      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Our Enemies” is the thirty-first prayer found in ברכה ותהלה <tei:hi rend="italic">Blessing and Praise: A Book of Meditations and Prayers for Individual and Home Devotion</tei:hi> (CCAR 1923), pp. 105-107. Unfortunately, we do not yet know of a resource providing clear attribution of authorship for any of the prayers in this volume. However, the pacifist language and argument in this prayer strongly identifies it as having been written by Rabbi Abraham Cronbach. For a comparative, find Rabbi Cronbach’s prayer, “Our Contemners” published in his own collection, <tei:hi rend="italic">Prayers of the Jewish Advance</tei:hi> (1924), pp. 8-11.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_66518_notes"/>
